/**
 * COLORECTAL (BOWEL) CANCER: LIVING WITH IT, CARE AND DECISIONS (UK and NHS focus). Facts checked 24 September 2026.
 *
 * The patient side of the colorectal record, written to the pancreatic and triple-negative standard
 * (./pancreatic-living.ts, ./tnbc-living.ts): ten decision rows the decisions page turns into sections (the operation
 * and what a stoma means; chemotherapy after surgery for stage 2 and stage 3 and how the benefit is worked out;
 * rectal cancer, surgery or chemoradiotherapy first and watch and wait; which first treatment for cancer that has
 * spread, by RAS, BRAF, mismatch repair and which side of the bowel; surgery for spread to the liver; immunotherapy
 * when the tumour is mismatch repair deficient; later lines when chemotherapy stops working; Lynch syndrome testing
 * and what it means for the family; a trial or standard treatment; when to talk about palliative care), the
 * hand-written question set the appointment sheet, prep pack and decision pages read (exported as
 * `colorectalQuestions`, wired in src/data/questions.ts), and living-with material attached as sourced notes and
 * links to the side-effect, procedure and support records other files own (bowel function and low anterior resection
 * syndrome, stoma care, diet, oxaliplatin neuropathy, hand-foot syndrome, irinotecan diarrhoea, the rash from the
 * EGFR antibodies, fatigue, sexual function and fertility, body image, work and money, carers).
 *
 * This file creates no glossary terms: the glossary pass (agent A) owns them. Drafts for the terms this material
 * wants are exported as `colorectalLivingTermDrafts`, written to the glossary standard so they can be registered by
 * spreading the array; the ids they use are referenced nowhere in the graph until then. Trials are owned by the
 * registry pass (agent B): rows here reference only trials already on the record (RAPIDO, PRODIGE 23, OPRA, PROSPECT,
 * the German rectal trial, KEYNOTE-177, CheckMate 8HW, NICHE-2, PARADIGM, CRYSTAL and FIRE-3, BREAKWATER, SUNLIGHT,
 * FRESCO-2, DYNAMIC, FOCUS4, AZUR-1, SABR-COMET).
 *
 * Every medical statement points at an NHS, Bowel Cancer UK, Macmillan, Cancer Research UK, Colostomy UK, Maggie's or
 * Marie Curie patient page, or at NICE NG151. Nothing here is advice for an individual: the pages say so and every
 * urgent card carries the team's own 24-hour number ahead of 111 and 999.
 */

